<title>INDIA: India's forex reserves rise to $23.79 bln on Nov 8.</title>
<headline>India's forex reserves rise to $23.79 bln on Nov 8.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves rose to $23.79 billion on November 8, 1996, from $23.58 billion the previous week, the Reserve Bank of India said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.</p>
<p>	 Foreign exchange reserves (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					   Nov 8	 Nov 1	 Nov 10</p>
<p>					    1996	  1996	   1995</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     19,330	19,126	 17,481</p>
<p>    Gold				 4,382	 4,382	  4,408</p>
<p>    SDRs				    76	    76	     34</p>
<p>    Total			     23,788	23,584	 21,923</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
